// College programs by sport, for every sport except basketball.
//
// Source: U.S. Department of Education, Equity in Athletics (EADA), 2024
// filing — https://ope.ed.gov/athletics/. Every institution receiving Title IV
// funding that runs an intercollegiate athletics programme reports its roster
// counts per sport, so a non-zero count is the school genuinely fielding that
// sport. That is the part we could not have invented: which colleges actually
// have a baseball team is a fact, not a guess.
//
// Basketball deliberately stays in college-data.js. That list is hand-curated
// and carries conference affiliations, which EADA does not publish — replacing
// it would trade real data for a longer list.
//
// Known limits, surfaced in the UI rather than hidden:
//   - 2024 filing, so roughly two years stale. Sponsorship moves slowly, but
//     programmes do get cut.
//   - Self-reported by each institution.
//   - No conference. EADA has no conference column at all.
//   - CCCAA (California) and NWAC (Northwest) community-college systems count
//     as JUCO. Institutions under NCCAA, USCAA, "Other" and Independent are
//     omitted — they don't map to a division an athlete filters by. This is
//     what makes baseball reconstruct to exactly 1588 from the raw filing.
//
// Shape: SPORT_SCHOOLS is [name, division, state]. SPORT_INDEX maps a sport
// key to positions in that array, so a school shared by six sports is stored
// once. No pre-built search URLs — the old file stored one per row and nothing
// ever read them.

